Building production AI agents across disparate frameworks creates unmaintainable fragmentation. Metaview previously maintained recruiting agents on Step Functions, LangGraph, and ad-hoc event loops, meaning every product had to re-solve sandboxing, session state, streaming, and model observability.

Rigid graph frameworks like LangGraph fail on open-ended customer workflows because developers must map every execution path ahead of time. When initial tool queries come back empty, pre-baked routing breaks down. Metaview solved this by consolidating all agents onto a single unified execution harness inspired by Ramp Inspect.

Under this pattern, every agent runs inside an isolated container sandbox with a real filesystem and bash execution capabilities, allowing the model to dynamically inspect data and plan its own intermediate steps. Standardizing on this harness dropped new agent setup time from days to under two hours.

Stop rebuilding custom plumbing for every prompt workflow. Provide the model with isolated system tools and a standardized execution environment instead of hardcoded state machines.

