Directly editing weights in neural networks to update facts usually causes catastrophic forgetting across adjacent knowledge bases. TopoVoid introduces a 212M parameter model architecture that isolates explicit concept bottlenecks, enabling factual edits via closed-form linear solvers rather than iterative gradient descent.

The framework reserves 176 out of 1024 residual dimensions for core concept activations. The remaining 82.8 percent forms an orthogonal null space. By projecting residual updates through this projection matrix, new facts can be written into attention and MLP projection weights while guaranteeing zero interference with protected concept spaces.

Instead of full-parameter fine-tuning or fragile prompt-based retrieval patches, this design frames model editing as a regularized linear system solve over key-value representations.

Architecting explicit null spaces directly into model representations provides a predictable foundation for real-time model updates without fine-tuning overhead.

